    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting high-upside matchups for our speed-first assets. **Mickey Moniak** leads our projections with an elite 74.79 score, benefiting significantly from a favorable platoon advantage against a right-handed arm and wind conditions shifting in his favor. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** secures a 71.87 rating; despite the left-on-left dynamic, the combination of his top-tier sprint speed and a high-probability SB environment against a pitcher with a slow delivery makes him a must-start staple in our OF2 slot.\n\nThe decision to bench **Cole Young** at 40.82 was the most contentious move of the morning. While **Cole Young** benefits from a favorable spot in the order and a slight boost for his SB potential against Seymour, he narrowly fell short of the efficiency threshold established by **Max Muncy** (53.71) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (51.73). Both **Max Muncy** and **Tyler Soderstrom** are being boosted by wind-assisted park factors and platoon advantages that push their production ceiling higher than the base projection for **Cole Young**. We are monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** closely; as their official lineups are still pending, our 57.98 and 52.49 estimates are contingent on them maintaining their projected #3 spots. If any of these \"lineup pending\" players drop significantly in the batting order, expect their daily efficiency scores to dip, forcing a late re-evaluation of the bench depth currently occupied by **Zach McKinstry** and the unavailable **Trevor Story**.",
